pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% One knob turned: the degree is `i64::MIN + 1` instead of `i64::MIN`, and nothing else changes.
% The substituted degree is then exactly `i64::MIN`, which still fits, so no contradicting row
% is produced and the UNFIXED checker refuses this proof as well. That is the causation
% argument: what forged the verdict is the WRAP, not the size of the numbers.
f 2;
rup 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775807 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
